---
// What a main page is for, in a sentence at its top (UI-24). It's about the page rather than part
// of it, so it doesn't stand out: white with a dark-blue shadow, straight on the gradient. That's
// an agreed exception to the contrast rule, and the look test that measures text on the gradient
// skips it. In a header row, such as Groups' with Start a group, it takes the room at the left.
---

<p class="page-sentence">
  <slot />
</p>

<style>
  .page-sentence {
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    color: white;
    font-size: 1.2em;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-shadow: 1px 2px var(--blue-dark);
  }
  :global(main > .top) > .page-sentence {
    flex: 1 1 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* The button beside it wraps onto two lines before it squeezes the sentence. */
  :global(main > .top) > .page-sentence ~ :global(*) {
    max-width: 45%;
  }
</style>
